  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "har or er?",
   "texto": "Almost always **har** + participle: Jeg **har** set dem.\n\nBut **er** is used if the verb **no lleva complemento directo** and expresses **movimiento o cambio**:\n\n- Han **er** kommet hjem. (has arrived)\n- Hun **er** rejst. (is gone)\n- Han **er** blevet tysker. (became German)\n\nIn the past: **havde** / **var** + participle.",
   "tutora": "pensando"
  },
